--
--   Description
--
-- This test is intended to cover the transmit functionality of the
-- GEM in gigabit operation when using the TBI (PCS layer) interface.
-- Half duplex operation is used throughout this test case. Input data
-- to the MAC is supplied via the external fifo interface.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
--
-- . Ensure link status interrupt is generated once synchronisation is
--   detected in the receive path.
--
-- . Ensure there are no errors in frames transmitted by the PCS in
--   half duplex mode when the MAC generates the first preamble of
--   a frame on either an odd or even code group boundary of the PCS.
--
-- · Ensure there are no errors in frames transmitted by the PCS in
--   half duplex mode that finish with both T/R/I and T/R/R/I.
--
-- . Ensure both I1 and I2 ordered sets are used correctly at end of
--   frame in half duplex mode.
--
-- . Ensure bursting and carrier extension is handled correctly by the
--   PCS when the MAC is operating in half duplex mode.
--  
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
--
-- The auto-negotiation function is disabled (using bit-7 of the PCS
-- Control Register) prior to selecting PCS. The PCS is selected
-- by setting the MAC into Gigabit mode and setting PCS enable in the
-- MAC network configuration register.
--
-- Wait for the link status interrupt.
--
-- SINGLE FRAME - FRAME 1.
--
-- Generate a single frame which is 52 bytes in length, padding, crc and
-- carrier extension are added by the mac layer (512 bytes in total).
-- Mac layer starts this transmission such that it aligns to an odd code
-- group boundary of the PCS, hence only 6 preamble are transmitted by the
-- PCS (the first replaced with /S).
-- The frame finishes with /T/R/R for even alignment and I1/I2 ordered sets
-- for maintaining disparity.
--
-- SINGLE FRAME - FRAME 2.
--
-- Generate a single frame which is 513 bytes in length including crc.
-- Mac layer starts this transmission such that it aligns to an even code
-- group boundary of the PCS, hence 7 preamble are transmitted by the
-- PCS (the first replaced with /S).
-- The frame finishes with /T/R/R for even alignment and I1/I2 ordered sets
-- for maintaining disparity.
--
-- SINGLE FRAME - FRAME 3.
--
-- Generate a single frame which is 65 bytes in length including crc, carrier
-- extension is applied to take the frame to 512 bytes.
-- Mac layer starts this transmission such that it aligns to an odd code group
-- boundary of the PCS, hence only 6 preamble are transmitted by the
-- PCS (the first replaced with /S).
-- The frame finishes with /T/R/R for even alignment and I2 ordered sets
-- for maintaining disparity.
--
-- SINGLE FRAME - FRAME 4.
--
-- Generate a single frame which is 512 bytes in length including crc.
-- Mac layer starts this transmission such that it aligns to an even code
-- group boundary of the PCS, hence 7 preamble are transmitted by the
-- PCS (the first replaced with /S).
-- The frame finishes with /T/R for even alignment and I2 ordered sets
-- for maintaining disparity.
--
-- BURST OF THREE FRAMES - BURST A.
--
-- First frame is 65 bytes in length including crc, carrier extension is
-- applied to extend the frame to 512 bytes. Mac layer starts this transmission
-- such that it aligns to an odd code group boundary of the PCS, hence only 6
-- preamble are transmitted by the PCS (the first replaced with /S).
--
-- Carrier extension is applied through ifg.
--
-- Second frame is 65 bytes in length including crc.
--
-- Carrier extension is applied through ifg.
--
-- Third frame is 65 bytes in length including crc. The frame finishes with
-- /T/R/R for even alignment and I1/I2 ordered sets for maintaining disparity.
--
-- BURST OF THREE FRAMES - BURST B.
--
-- First frame is 64 bytes in length including crc, carrier extension is
-- applied to extend the frame to 512 bytes. Mac layer starts this transmission
-- such that it aligns to an even code group boundary of the PCS, hence 7
-- preamble are transmitted by the PCS (the first replaced with /S).
--
-- Carrier extension is applied through ifg.
--
-- Second frame is 65 bytes in length including crc.
--
-- Carrier extension is applied through ifg.
--
-- Third frame is 65 bytes in length including crc. The frame finishes with
-- /T/R for even alignment and I1/I2 ordered sets for maintaining disparity.
--
-- Check the statistics registers.
--
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Configuration Requirements ..
requires ext_fifo_interface 1
requires no_pcs 0
pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state


-- check the relevant pcs registers
apbrd(100) 184 00000000 -- ignore this read


-- this is the event count that will initialize the scaler for event counts. it will cause any future scaling to only scale
-- the counts after start_scale
start_scale

                         -- indicates the pcs is in reset (until enabled)
apbrd      204 00000109  -- check reset value of pcs status reg
apbrd      210 00000020  -- check reset value of pcs a-n advertisement reg
apbrd      214 00000000  -- check reset value of pcs a-n link ptnr ability reg
apbrd      218 00000004  -- check reset value of pcs a-n expansion reg
apbrd      21C 00000000  -- check reset value of pcs a-n next page reg
apbrd      220 00000000  -- check reset value of pcs a-n link partner reg
apbrd      23C 00008000  -- check reset value of pcs a-n extended status reg


-- initialise the relevant pcs registers
apbwr      200 00000040  -- disable auto-negotiation prior to enabling PCS


-- check and initialise the relevant mac registers
apbrd      000 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbwr      028 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      008 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register

-- # Initialize the network configuration register
-- #   -eam      <1|0|random>, default = 0. This is external address matching
-- #   -duplex   <full|half|random>, default = random
-- #   -speed    <1g|100m|10m|random>, default = random
-- #   -jumbo    <1|0|random>, default = random. This wont affect the RX transactor below, but will automatically cause jumbos to be dropped.
-- #   -copy_all <1|0|random>, default = 0. If 0, ensure you initialize the dest_addr in the rx transactor to something that will match
-- #   -databus  <32|64|128|take_from_cfg|random>, default = random, bus <= config.  The max value is the value set in dma_bus_width in gem_defs.v
-- #   -rx_toe   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables RX TCP/IP checksum offload
-- #   -pcs_en   <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables SGMII PCS
-- #   -pause_en <1|0|random>, default = 0. Enables pausing of transmission
-- #   -dont_copy_pause <1|0|random>, default = 0. Controls whether pause frames are copied
init_ncr -sgmii_en 0 -pcs_en 1 -retry_test 0 -copy_all 0 -duplex half -speed 1g -jumbo 0 -databus 32 -eam 0 -rx_toe 0 -pause_en 0 -dont_copy_pause 0 -multicast_hash 0 -unicast_hash 0


apbrd(int)  24 00000200  -- check link status change interrupt
apbwr       24 ffffffff  -- clear interrupt
apbwrf     000 00000008  -- enable tx (apb trigger to trigger fifo)

